# `lti::Gram`

## Signature

```cpp
lti::Gram lti::Gram::Reach;
lti::Gram lti::Gram::Observe;
```

## What It Does

Selects which energy Gramian `lti::gram` computes. The choice changes both the Lyapunov driver and, for observability, the orientation of the dynamics matrix.

## Fields

| Field | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `Reach` | Reachability or controllability Gramian, driven by `B Bᴴ`. |
| `Observe` | Observability Gramian, driven by `Cᴴ C`. |

## Returns

Pass one enumerator as the `side` argument to `lti::gram`; the enum does not allocate a matrix itself.

## Errors

Both choices require dynamics for which the corresponding continuous or discrete Lyapunov equation has a well-conditioned solution.

